00:01:41.557 --> 00:01:43.080
- Yeah.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:43.913
- Oh, my God.

00:01:43.913 --> 00:01:45.630
I love when you come.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:46.830
- [Joel] This is so great.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:47.910
Kelly doesn't care.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:49.960
This is great 'cause we're like-

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:50.793
Aw.

00:01:50.793 --> 00:01:53.003
- [Kelly] Who cares about
Joel when there's animals.

00:01:54.308 --> 00:01:55.141
- [Joel] There you go.

00:01:55.141 --> 00:01:55.974
Look at that, guys.

00:01:55.974 --> 00:01:57.510
Have you ever seen anything this cute?

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:02.220
And a lot of people think
they're, you know, they smell.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:03.053
They don't.

00:02:03.053 --> 00:02:05.023
- They don't smell.
- They smell like jasmine.

00:02:05.023 --> 00:02:07.440
They don't smell like jasmine.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.242
You just walked right into it.

00:02:09.242 --> 00:02:10.620
- [Kelly] Probably because
it's hard to clean themselves.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.063
They're so slow about it.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.040
- They're a little slow, but you know,

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.320
they are three times
stronger than a human being.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.700
And I am not kidding.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.300
They can basically hang
from a tree indefinitely.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.740
- Oh, my gosh.
- No joke.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.900
- So wait, so what happens
on the show "Animal Control?"

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:25.733
What happens?

00:02:25.733 --> 00:02:27.113
- I don't know, I can't remember.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.420
I think it takes place in space.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.520
No, it's called "Animal Control."

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.560
And it's about the people
that come to your...

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:35.670
if you call them, they're like,

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.980
there's a raccoon or a coyote

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.110
or a snake in your backyard

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:43.140
or somebody's got an illegal rabbit farm

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:43.973
or something,

00:02:43.973 --> 00:02:46.140
we come and take those things away.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.480
It's an office... office...

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.960
A comedy, and the cast is fantastic.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.497
Obviously.

00:02:53.497 --> 00:02:54.330
- That's gotta be fun.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:57.390
You go to work and
there's animals everyday.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:58.223
- Yeah.

00:02:58.223 --> 00:02:59.910
- What's the coolest
animal that's been on set

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:01.860
that you were like, oh,
that was a cool experience.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.420
- The tarantula was pretty great.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:04.560
- [Kelly] I like tarantulas.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:05.393
- Yeah.

00:03:05.393 --> 00:03:07.380
- I heard that, wait, did
it crawl on your face?

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.730
- I let it crawl on my face.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.353
Do we have... there it is, yeah.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.710
That is a seven-year-old
tarantula named Gretchen.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:14.763
I'm not kidding.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.240
And if you stop thinking...

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.080
people are like, isn't it scary?

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.860
It just feels like somebody
just very lightly crawling

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:25.170
across your face with fangs that big.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.003
- Yeah.

00:03:26.909 --> 00:03:28.527
But not poisonous.

00:03:28.527 --> 00:03:31.110
- No, they say it feels like a bee sting.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.613
Which it didn't sting me.

00:03:33.547 --> 00:03:37.620
That particular tarantula is
handled by children every day.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.030
And I'm not kidding.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:39.863
- I'm not kidding.

00:03:39.863 --> 00:03:41.070
I grew up...

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.270
When I was young, I went to this school

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:45.270
and there were just tarantulas everywhere.

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:46.770
Like in the whole...

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:48.810
It was a very poor area.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:50.100
And literally there were tarantulas

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.030
and they would come outta the holes.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.183
I'm not kidding, we'd
play with 'em at recess.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:56.490
- They're like, "Sorry,
we don't have a big toy."

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:57.717
Just play with the tarantula.

00:03:57.717 --> 00:03:59.820
- But I'm telling you what's
interesting though for kids,

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:02.670
like you could have put the
most wonderful playground

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.050
ever out there, but you know,

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.390
it's awesome that its like,
tarantulas are out there.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.680
- And they live in the ground.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.720
- Yeah, there were giant holes everywhere.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.760
And literally that's what I
remember from that school.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.130
- What was the school mascot?

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.210
- Bees, Luella Merrett.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:16.320
Bees.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.660
But you know what, the tarantula
sting feels like a bee.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.010
So we weren't far off.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:20.910
I listened.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:22.140
- Where was the school?

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:23.880
- Fort Worth, Texas.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:27.120
So has this new show made
you wanna get more pets?

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.830
Because every time you're here,

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.540
I feel like you almost get
in trouble with your wife

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.220
'cause you wanna bring an animal home?

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:35.340
- Yeah, I brought home a Clydesdale horse.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:36.173
- Did you really?

00:04:36.173 --> 00:04:37.380
- No!
- Oh.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:38.850
- Clydesdales are like awesome.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:39.960
- Yes, they're huge though.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:40.793
- They're massive.

00:04:40.793 --> 00:04:42.840
One of the largest horse breeds, guys.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:46.080
- You're like Nat Geo.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:49.110
- Well, there was a puppy that I was like,

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:51.570
I've gotta find a way to bring this home.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:54.127
And then I told my wife and she was like,

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:57.900
"Don't come home because
you've already brought-"

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.553
We have three dogs and a rabbit.

00:05:01.204 --> 00:05:02.820
And she's like, "We have enough."

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:03.750
We have a small-

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.730
- I have two dogs and three rabbits.

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:07.290
And a hamster.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:08.123
It's a lot.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.323
- I can't top that.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.260
Well, I got two teenagers.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:14.760
- I have a six and eight-year-old.

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:15.720
- Ugh.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:16.620
Okay.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.050
- Wait, speaking of teenagers, he's 18.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:19.883
Eddie, right?

00:05:19.883 --> 00:05:21.570
- Yes, my son turned 18.

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:22.470
- So wait, 18.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:23.810
Do you feel like...

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.940
You have an adult kid.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:27.870
Do you feel old?

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:28.920
This is what I wanna ask.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.230
- Yes, I feel very old.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.050
I bought him a pack of
cigarettes, just for fun.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.400
I'm kidding.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.350
Smoking is terrible for you.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:38.880
It was cigars and, uh...

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.620
No.
- Classy.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:41.970
- It's very weird.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:42.803
Yeah, there he is.

00:05:42.803 --> 00:05:44.460
He looks really happy to be at Stonehenge.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:45.930
That's where we were.

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:46.763
- I've never done that.

00:05:46.763 --> 00:05:48.270
That's cool.
- It is cool.

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:49.103
- Yeah.

00:05:49.103 --> 00:05:50.437
Except when the kids
get there, they're like,

00:05:50.437 --> 00:05:51.547
"Wow."

00:05:51.547 --> 00:05:53.187
"Rocks."

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:56.610
You'd probably much rather
have some tarantulas.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:59.010
Yeah, now he's like a man.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:02.550
I mean he's got the hair of a man.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:03.720
Got hair everywhere.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:06.060
And yeah, he smells like a man.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:06.893
- Strange, yeah.

00:06:06.893 --> 00:06:08.370
Total adult, yeah.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:09.240
- You'll see.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:11.274
And it'll happen before you know it.

00:06:11.274 --> 00:06:12.107
- I know.

00:06:12.107 --> 00:06:14.100
- I mean, these people
grew before our very eyes.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.450
- Just now.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:18.030
- They start out a fun kids audience.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:19.080
And now look at 'em.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.460
- It was romper room and now it's-

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.710
- How do the clothes still
fit them is the real question.

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:23.760
- Wait, so you and your wife,

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:24.593
this is amazing,

00:06:24.593 --> 00:06:26.640
26th anniversary, did
y'all just celebrated?

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:27.900
- Well, last summer, 26.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:29.314
We're coming up to 27.
- That's incredible.

00:06:29.314 --> 00:06:32.880
(audience applauding)

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:35.060
- There we are.
- Y'all are so cute.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:35.893
Do you still...

00:06:35.893 --> 00:06:38.550
At this point, do you still do gifts?

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:41.070
I mean, what do you get
each other at this point?

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:43.050
- I got her a sloth and-

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:45.180
- She's so stoked about it.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:47.160
- We have not...

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.270
It's one of those things

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:51.780
where she's tried a bunch
of times to buy me clothes

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:54.690
and she's like, "I'm not gonna try."

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:58.310
But for my birthday, she got me...

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:02.078
You know Brian Cox from
"Succession" on HBO?

00:07:02.078 --> 00:07:02.911
- Yeah.

00:07:02.911 --> 00:07:05.843
- We got a cameo of him
telling me to (bleep) off.

00:07:05.843 --> 00:07:08.790
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:10.560
I kind of cried a little bit.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.390
I was like this is the greatest thing

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:14.130
I've ever received as a gift.

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:16.263
- What a perfect counterpart for you.

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:18.777
- She was like, "Here you go."

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:21.570
- I bought her a coat last week

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:22.800
where I just kind of saw it

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:24.210
and I was like, "This looks good."

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.710
And I purchased it.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.397
It arrived and she was like,

00:07:27.397 --> 00:07:28.710
"This actually works."

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.510
And it was a surprise.

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.250
- It's hard to do
clothes for other people.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.990
- It is, yeah.

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:35.940
- And she's always like,
"Oh, this is actually good."

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:38.820
As if... everything else was kind of-

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:39.780
- Crap.
- Crappy.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:42.213
And so she likes it, so yeah.

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:44.430
We suck at dating.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.800
Our first date was in like in '93.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:47.633
So...

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:51.360
Yeah, when the photographer
was not even born.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.310
And yeah, we look at each other,

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:55.797
we're like, where did all this-?

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.020
- [Kelly] Time?

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.737
To this day, when I get
in bed with her, I'm like,

00:07:59.737 --> 00:08:01.407
"I'm in bed with a lady."

00:08:03.113 --> 00:08:04.140
- With my lady friend.
- Look at her.

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:05.193
Woo, what happened?

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:07.410
- That's why you're still together.

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:08.550
That's awesome.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:11.310
At least you're not looking
over going, "You again."

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:12.333
- She does that.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:16.440
Her eyes can roll all the way over.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:17.370
And she doesn't really...

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:20.910
Well, she laughs at like every 50th joke.

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:22.590
And she'll be like, "Oh, that was funny."

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:23.997
- Because she's used to you.

00:08:23.997 --> 00:08:24.830
- Well, yes.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:26.880
- She probably knows what
joke you're gonna say.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.620
- Well, sometimes.

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:30.600
Or I'm just relentlessly annoying.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:32.970
But I, like, dated a
girl once that laughed

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:33.810
at everything I said.

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:35.970
And I was like, this is weird.

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:37.485
I shouldn't be winning this much.

00:08:37.485 --> 00:08:38.318
- I know, but you're funny.

00:08:38.318 --> 00:08:40.200
That's on you, not her.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.580
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:42.540
That's your fault.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:44.090
- Yeah, that was Nicole Kidman.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:47.130
- Just like Jimmy Fallon

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.750
when he didn't know he was on a date.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:49.680
Did you see that?

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:50.513
- No.
- Oh, my god.

00:08:50.513 --> 00:08:52.170
This is a real thing.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.510
Nicole Kidman was on- did y'all see that?

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:56.340
And she was like, "No, we were on a date."

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:57.810
And he was like, "Wait, what?"

00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:01.080
And he had no idea he was on
a date with Nicole Kidman.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:01.950
- Really?
- The best.

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:03.360
